00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.897
So the way the
product works is--

00:10:47.897 --> 00:10:48.980
this is how it looks like.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:50.910
You have a tool
here in the cloud,

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:53.540
which you use to manage
all of the edge devices.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.430
The software runs on
the edge device itself.

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:58.400
We have a very flexible
microservices-based

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.487
architecture.

00:10:59.487 --> 00:11:01.820
In the traditional Linux
world, we have used containers.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:03.778
Obviously, in Android,
there are no containers.

00:11:03.778 --> 00:11:05.870
So we have developed
all of this as an app.

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:08.690
So the notion that
you can have all kinds

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.780
of data that fed into our
system through a database

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:12.790
that we have--

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:16.330
the two core key components
here are the analytics engine

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.380
and the edge ML, the
machine running engine.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:21.380
The idea being that as
you're ingesting live data

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.180
from all different
sources, you can

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:26.300
apply analytics and machine
learning on the data

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:27.740
to drive the insights.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:30.590
And then you can take
closed loop control actions

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:32.710
by either using our SDK.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.690
There is an SDK using which
you can build applications.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:38.660
Or you can also visualize
it and send that information

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:43.580
into IoT Core and
other places as well.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:46.080
So maybe let's
step back a second.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.120
A lot of you, I'm sure--

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.650
many of you are familiar
